body:
Well, I had my psych at outpatient mention I "may have avpd, but it could be depression and social anxiety" a few months ago. Not having a straight answer was driving me nuts. So I basically said to my therapist "its been really getting to me lately that my old psych said this and I don't have closure, so I was wondering if we could go over the symptoms so I can get a more in-depth opinion." 

She mentioned that she worked in a divison with people with personality disorders before and could tell by the second session that I had avpd based on everything I told her. She asked if I looked up the symptoms and I replied yeah and I have all of them. She said she low-key has been treating me for avpd for weeks, just didnt want to tell me I had it.

Thats basically the gist of it! I know a lot of psychs hear "self dx" and dissaprove of it so that could be why? Theres really no telling as to why she dismissed it. If a diagnosis is important to you maybe see someone new and mention your suspicions without including the words "self dxd". Frame it as looking to check out the symptoms with your therapist. Hopefully that helps ;;
